{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/95455-terrible-form-merit","id":95455,"title":"Terrible Form Merit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-21T01:16:36-07:00","id":95455,"title":"Terrible Form Merit","content":"Another quick question! Can a Demon take more than one instance of Terrible Form? There's nothing to say you <i>can't</i>, but I assume as a Style Merit the answer would be no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T01:22:53-07:00","id":95458,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that'd be a no(of course, barring Storyteller's discretion). Styles aren't repeatable, and it'd be too cheap a way to just stack on the demonic form abilities, completely negating the extra features you get as you go up in Primum(and therefore cheapening the appeal). Asides from becoming a switch army knife of a monster, there's also the absurd bonus you'd get to your compromise roll for partial transformations.<br /> <br /> Yeah, just no.<br /> <br /> EDIT: While the Primum raising is a bit of a bugbear, it seems to me that if you need more than 5 Mods, 4 Techs, 2 Props, and 3 Procs, you're not utilizing the tools you have well enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-21-2014, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T04:30:25-07:00","id":95508,"title":"","content":"Its considered a Style, on the same par as a Fighting or Debate style. Or Parkour. I wouldn't allow someone to buy Parkour twice, and stack the bonuses.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T06:57:40-07:00","id":95576,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I did a one-shot where one of the players took all four dots in Terrible Form.<br /> <br /> He was practically getting exceptionals every time on the partial transformation and he had more than he could shake a stick at. It was a sight to behold, but interesting.<br /> <br /> It doesn't need to be repeatable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T07:39:46-07:00","id":95619,"title":"","content":"That compromise roll for form parts is an issue, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T08:36:35-07:00","id":95667,"title":"","content":"I agree that it is an issue, but one that is easily solved with houseruling. Personally I'm considering allowing it once per session or not allowing the extra bonus from Terrible Form powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2001-tyler-foss","name":"Tyler Foss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T09:26:31-07:00","id":95695,"title":"","content":"I just run the partial transformation as though they didn't have the merit. Otherwise my PCs (who were ALL interested in the terrible form merit--its more appealing than mummy's necessary tomb, cult, and relic merits) would all have negligible compromise rolls to get most of the powers a non-Terrible PC could get going full mode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T11:37:05-07:00","id":95803,"title":"","content":"Yeah I am not too happy about the partial transformation compromise rolls. I was thinking of playing it so that the +1/Form bonus is on top of the -3 penalty for the full transformation. It kind of makes slightly more sense to me. Otherwise, say you have terrible form and you manifest all but one power. You are clearly an inhuman monstrosity and yet you have +1 bonus. And then if you manifest that extra form you suddenly have -3, for a sudden jump of 4 dice. Which seems odd to me. But if you add the +1/Form on top of the -3 penalty, the effect is &quot;smoother&quot;. Haven't tested it yet though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T11:56:43-07:00","id":95818,"title":"","content":"There is a bunch of additional costs to manifesting all but one power that make the 4 die difference a lot less of an issue. You have to spend an Aether for every 2 powers (assuming you took the merit for this knowing you want to manifest a lot of powers). And you also don't get the healing or Aether recharge that comes from manifesting full demon form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1105-hulsmanm","name":"hulsmanm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T21:01:08-07:00","id":96154,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'm considering just giving the merit out for free or something similar, or else disallowing it altogether. I don't like it as is. I suppose if I give something similar to my players I need to do something about partial transformations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T21:26:55-07:00","id":96163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/95455-terrible-form-merit?p=96154#post96154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I'm considering just giving the merit out for free or something similar, or else disallowing it altogether. I don't like it as is. I suppose if I give something similar to my players I need to do something about partial transformations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a somewhat related feeling to this.<br /> Every demon player I've gamed with so far has either began the game with Terrible Form or they have planned to acquire it (and then actually proceeded to do so) in very, very short order.<br /> I found that if the merit is universally acquired by all the players it is very, very good or considered a necessity. I'm still debating whether I want to just give it out for free, but I think I will, eventually and work that into the wider narrative. Why? I believe it'would yield more interesting character growth and a more interesting narrative if the players could spend those dots on more character-specific merits. . <br /> <br /> The partial transformation matter has been house-ruled as a straight up &quot;you never get a beat for exceptional successes for partial transformation. However, I will always give you an extra beat every session.&quot; So a possibly exploitable source of beats has been addressed with a regular pay-off to all the players for giving up something they should have RAW. Yes, it is more experiences overall, but since the bonus is predictable I can more easily figure that into my plans.<br /> I've had no complaints thus far.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","name":"Rixx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T04:44:52-07:00","id":96272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rixx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/95455-terrible-form-merit?p=96163#post96163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found that if the merit is universally acquired by all the players it is very, very good or considered a necessity. I'm still debating whether I want to just give it out for free, but I think I will, eventually and work that into the wider narrative. Why? I believe it'would yield more interesting character growth and a more interesting narrative if the players could spend those dots on more character-specific merits. .</div> </div> </div> </div> While I won't say its a necessity...<br /> <br /> Demon form and Exploits are the &quot;demon&quot; feeling powers of the game. You want more of them because, unlike Embeds, you tend to feel like an actual demon using them. And, unlike Exploits, you can get demon form abilities without needing to buy what some may consider an xp sink in Embed form*.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the arbitrary restriction on the number of the simultaneously powerful and thematic demon form abilities only increases their appeal. There's a lot of players out there that would be happy never getting an Embed or Exploit, and just learning new demon form abilities if they could buy them a bit more regularly than every few Premium levels. Or had more of a choice at those odd levels.<br /> <br /> It comes down to being a cheap method of getting powerful and flavorful abilities that has a very strong restriction on gaining said abilities in every other way. If the merit was eliminated, and you were getting new Form abilities at every Premium dot instead, I'm sure there wouldn't be grumbling, but more than a few players would be investing in high premium asap.<br /> <br /> <br /> * I'm calling Emebds an xp-sink because there are some styles of play where a chance to use Embeds simply don't come up as often in. Its something that you very well may not want to get on its own, but need for an Exploit. This isn't always true, of course. I wouldn't even necessarily call it default. But I know a lot of people who are more than ambivalent about most Embeds, and don't care about buying them. <br /> <br /> EDIT - Or they're looking at what Exploits they want, and what other Embed they can buy as justification instead of the suggested ones.<br /> <br /> Its like, when Vampire was being remade into Blood and Smoke, they made sure that all the disciplines from the first dot were evocative, useful, and monstrous. Embeds, as a power prerequisite, fail that test for a number of people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T15:26:36-07:00","id":96562,"title":"","content":"I don't know about you, but I pretty much only paid attention to Embeds for a long time. They fit my play style way more than Exploits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T16:33:02-07:00","id":96577,"title":"","content":"Ditto. Manipulative, subtle, insidiously effective when used right. Just the sort of thing a demon should be using.<br /> (not to mention that it feels highly thematic for me that demons would be subverting the very base-code of the universe in such a fashion)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T17:50:03-07:00","id":96608,"title":"","content":"And a third. Partial transformations do factor into that equation, but a majority of the scenarios in my head were always resolved by Embeds. I just think there's something cool about the quietness of them though. Heck, even fight scenes seem more interesting to me with liberal embed use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T18:22:00-07:00","id":96628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/95455-terrible-form-merit?p=96562#post96562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about you, but I pretty much only paid attention to Embeds for a long time. They fit my play style way more than Exploits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'm not saying they won't. There are some players for whom the reverse is true. They have a playstyle that fits the Exploits more than Embeds. For THEM, its an xp sink, as they don't want it.<br /> <br /> I didn't mean to imply that no one liked Embeds. Just that there are a number of people who don't like it. When I like playing a game, I like feeling like a monster out of the gate. I want to be a ghostly revenant in GtSE. I want to be a cackling witch in MtAw. When I play Demon, I want to feel more like a fallen angel. Embeds lend themselves to the sneaky spy style of play, and not the fallen angel or demon. That's not me, and I'm not always a fan of the embeds. And I know I'm not the only player who feels that way.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tell me, when you're focusing on gathering Embeds, do you feel like you should invest in Terrible Form as much? Its one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T22:58:32-07:00","id":98120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/95455-terrible-form-merit?p=96628#post96628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tell me, when you're focusing on gathering Embeds, do you feel like you should invest in Terrible Form as much?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends. Having a backup weapon like Demonic form is always good to have under your belt, and Terrible Form is all about making that weapon better.<br /> <br /> It's mostly from a GM and a design perspective that I dislike the merit, though. I'd personally rather make the Demonic Forms uniform in terms of how many components are available to each demon instead of keeping it as is.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T23:18:26-07:00","id":98134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/95455-terrible-form-merit?p=98120#post98120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends. Having a backup weapon like Demonic form is always good to have under your belt, and Terrible Form is all about making that weapon better.<br /> <br /> It's mostly from a GM and a design perspective that I dislike the merit, though. I'd personally rather make the Demonic Forms uniform in terms of how many components are available to each demon instead of keeping it as is.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my case virtually every character that I've put Terrible Form on as a starting Merit I very quickly found was more difficult to develop than with, say, the Social Merits that I eventually switched it for. It's useful for if, say, I have to have a second Propulsion, but all in all the drop-and-add element of form customization has been a fun exercise compared to just trying to staple on extra effects at the very beginning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}